---
import AboutHeroImage from '../assets/me.jpg';
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About Tefi — Crossing Dreams"
	description="I'm Tefi, an AI developer from Mexico. This is my little corner of the internet — GKS, Korean, life, and everything else."
	pubDate={new Date('March 18 2026')}
	heroImage={AboutHeroImage}
>
	<p>
		Hi! I'm Tefi — an AI developer from western Mexico, 24 years old, and currently in that stage
		of life where it feels like everything is moving too fast and not fast enough at the same time.
		You probably know the feeling.
	</p>

	<p>
		By day I build things with AI. I studied systems engineering, which means my brain naturally
		goes to structure, logic, and problem-solving — but the rest of me is somewhere between a
		manhwa chapter, a guitar riff, and a really good run.
	</p>

	<div class="currently-card">
		<p class="currently-title">✦ &nbsp; currently</p>
		<div class="currently-grid">
			<div class="currently-item">
				<span class="currently-label">studying</span>
				<span class="currently-value rotating" data-values='["Korean A2 · waiting for GKS interview", "systems thinking + AI pipelines", "how to say 괜찮아 without accent"]'></span>
			</div>
			<div class="currently-item">
				<span class="currently-label">watching</span>
				<span class="currently-value rotating" data-values='["One Piece T2", "old K-drama comfort rewatches", "every GKS interview vlog I can find"]'></span>
			</div>
			<div class="currently-item">
				<span class="currently-label">listening</span>
				<span class="currently-value rotating" data-values='["Autumn Morning — IU", "Lilac — IU", "Strawberry Moon — IU", "eight — IU ft. Suga"]'></span>
			</div>
			<div class="currently-item">
				<span class="currently-label">dreaming of</span>
				<span class="currently-value rotating" data-values='["빙수 in Korea", "a window seat on a flight to Seoul", "편의점 at 2am", "speaking Korean without thinking first"]'></span>
			</div>
			<div class="currently-item">
				<span class="currently-label">working on</span>
				<span class="currently-value rotating" data-values='["showing up, even on the hard days", "this blog, one post at a time", "being patient with the process"]'></span>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>

	<script is:inline>
		document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () {
			var items = document.querySelectorAll('.currently-value.rotating');
			var indexes = [];

			items.forEach(function (el, i) {
				var values = JSON.parse(el.dataset.values || '[]');
				indexes[i] = 0;
				el.textContent = values[0];

				setTimeout(function () {
					setInterval(function () {
						indexes[i] = (indexes[i] + 1) % values.length;
						el.classList.add('fade-out');
						setTimeout(function () {
							el.textContent = values[indexes[i]];
							el.classList.remove('fade-out');
						}, 350);
					}, 6000);
				}, i * 700);
			});
		});
	</script>

	<h2>How Korea Entered My Life</h2>

	<p>
		It started with a bingsu stand. There was a Korean woman in my city who sold 빙수, and some
		options came with red bean paste — the real kind. I don't know how to explain it except that
		the place felt like a secret. Like something just mine. Warm and a little magical, tucked into
		an ordinary afternoon.
	</p>

	<p>
		From there it snowballed — dramas, music, the language, the culture, the food, the way Korea
		holds ancient and modern in the same breath. And eventually: the GKS scholarship. A chance to
		actually go. To study there. To turn the feeling from that little bingsu stand into something
		real.
	</p>

	<h2>What This Blog Is</h2>

	<p>
		<strong>Crossing Dreams</strong> is my little corner of the internet. Yes, there's a lot about
		the GKS scholarship (everything I wish I'd found when I was searching). But also: learning
		Korean from zero, being a developer in your twenties, books I'm reading, things I'm making,
		random thoughts that deserve more than a tweet, and whatever else is living in my head.
	</p>

	<p>
		I write the way I'd talk to a friend. No filters, no expert positioning. Just honest notes from
		someone figuring it out as she goes.
	</p>

	<p>
		If any of this resonates — whether you're chasing something big, learning something hard, or
		just want company while you figure things out — welcome.
	</p>
</Layout>

<style>
	.currently-card {
		background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--pink-soft), var(--white));
		border: 1px solid var(--border);
		border-radius: 20px;
		padding: 1.4em 1.6em;
		margin: 0.5em 0 2.5em;
	}

	.currently-title {
		font-family: var(--font-body);
		font-size: 0.72em;
		font-weight: 600;
		letter-spacing: 0.12em;
		color: var(--pink-dark);
		text-transform: uppercase;
		margin: 0 0 1em;
	}

	.currently-grid {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.6em;
	}

	.currently-item {
		display: flex;
		gap: 0.8em;
		align-items: baseline;
	}

	.currently-label {
		font-family: var(--font-body);
		font-size: 0.75em;
		font-weight: 600;
		color: var(--pink-dark);
		min-width: 90px;
		letter-spacing: 0.04em;
	}

	.currently-value {
		font-family: var(--font-heading);
		font-size: 1em;
		color: var(--text);
		font-style: italic;
		transition: opacity 0.35s ease;
	}

	.currently-value.fade-out {
		opacity: 0;
	}
</style>
